# What `deploy/node/Dockerfile` does not need from the build context.
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` shipped the whole checkout, and on a CI runner that
# had just run `cargo build` the context was 1.68 GB of `target/` -- artifacts the
# image could not reuse anyway, because cargo's fingerprints are keyed on absolute
# paths and `/src` is not `/home/runner/work/...`. The from-source build needs the
# manifests, the lockfile, the toolchain file, every crate directory (the workspace
# manifest names them all, `gungnir-fuzz` included through `exclude`), and the
# license files the runtime stage copies. Nothing else.
target/
**/target/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
docs/
testdata/
benches/
